hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27609","Haddathana Abd al-Samad, he said: Haddathana Bashshar ibn Abd al-Malik, and he said: Umm Hakim bint Dinar narrated to me from her freedwoman Umm Ishaq that she was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a bowl of tharid was brought, and she ate with him, and Dhu al-Yadayn was with him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, handed her a bone and said: O Umm Ishaq, take of this. Then she remembered that she was fasting, so she drew back her hand, neither putting it forward nor back. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: What is wrong with you? She said: I was fasting but I forgot. Then Dhu al-Yadayn said: Now, after you have eaten your fill? So the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Complete your fast, for it is only provision that Allah brought to you."
